#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059469 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/id #uuid "d2698dbf-dea6-5abb-970e-a3ace180e337" :question/math-academy-id "e-4341" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059470 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/id #uuid "b834e666-de4f-5964-a280-6571ad44b6bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4343" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aac8c206-b291-573d-ae2a-74259dfb0e6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle  - 28,-19,-61\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056528} {:answer/id #uuid "ca53652c-eb08-5737-b6e1-44c670d816d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle  - 18, 19,-61\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056529} {:answer/id #uuid "f956129b-c0d4-5106-85ef-d4cae79b9a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle  - 28, 19,-19\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056530} {:answer/id #uuid "5c983fbc-29f4-567c-af19-bcd23d5769f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 28,-19,-19\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056531} {:answer/id #uuid "69487641-8222-5353-80f9-06c01524c50c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 18, 19, 61\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca53652c-eb08-5737-b6e1-44c670d816d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle  - 18, 19,-61\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056529} :answer-field/id #uuid "55babe7a-df9e-5246-9069-b8e548bbfc62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056527}] :question/id #uuid "7427d773-9726-5cf6-8261-06dbd4949f9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-1405" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{u} = \\langle  - 3 , 10 , 4 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle  4 , 7 , 1 \\rangle  .$. Find $u \\cdot v$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dcb1cbd-94dd-5ec7-a370-51627c867ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dcb1cbd-94dd-5ec7-a370-51627c867ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304181} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb4ef77-6cb3-5d3f-b4c1-653cc0729217" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dee8668-d5bd-5bbb-8e15-abc9e8c4f1ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dee8668-d5bd-5bbb-8e15-abc9e8c4f1ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304183} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b2f2c49-3c37-5b34-953e-85c4bdac5471" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "077d8348-aacc-5cfe-9c4f-83cd2cce459b" :question/math-academy-id "q-282278" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{157}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(4x-12)j+(0-3)k \\\\  & =⟨2,12-4x,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(12-4x)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(144-96x+16{x}^{2})+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157} & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x+157 & =157 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x & =0 \\\\ 16x(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75b4e25f-1030-5b07-89ea-2c0a3d618edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304186} {:answer/id #uuid "67d14441-a0c9-5061-a93c-e5acee68411f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304187} {:answer/id #uuid "69682917-4196-5bce-8932-d2047ba4f27f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304188} {:answer/id #uuid "2cb2ab75-866a-5bcb-b308-7f16325a231f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304189} {:answer/id #uuid "e51be6ff-88ca-52a1-b0ad-255306fa8a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cb2ab75-866a-5bcb-b308-7f16325a231f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304189} :answer-field/id #uuid "87a9aae2-c040-564a-9d2d-e42640d1113c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54ac0cd9-756f-56ec-a02b-bc51faafb7b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-77427" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,x,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,-x,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=10.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3x+x)i-(6-1)j+(-2x-x)k \\\\  & =⟨4x,-5,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+25+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =10 \\\\ \\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)} & =10 \\\\ 25({x}^{2}+1) & =100 \\\\ {x}^{2}+1 & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}.$"}]}
